CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ calls: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ partial specialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The parser moves a member's trailing return type into the declaration's
type, which the class body type-checked before the member's parameters
existed: `decltype(obj)' failed with "symbol 'obj' is unknown".
